<http://data.silknow.org/object/6f29abd1-e522-33d8-b855-907dd77c3512/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Sampler, linen embroidered with silk in double running  variations and combinations, mushabak and satin stitch filling in squares, and with metal thread in double running in a line, half cross stitch worked over a laid thread and satin stitch.\nThe motifs are worked in many different directions and colours. In one corner is a group of three cypress tress with a building to their right which has two domes. In another corner is a narrow necked blue vase containing a single pink flower."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6f29abd1-e522-33d8-b855-907dd77c3512> .

